# Every elimination a remainder walk passed through, carried into the root's unit. One row per
# (composed layer, quantity), summed over every intermediate the walk ran through, read at the
# corner of the quantity it was counted in.
#
# Empty when every walk stops at depth one
#   It is empty whenever every walk stops at depth one, which is almost always. A settled node's
#   filed totals already carry every correction its own composer applied, so stopping there needs
#   nothing from this relation. Rows appear only where a walk ran past a node, which happens
#   exactly where that node's own conversions have width, and the corrections it applied were
#   bypassed with its filed figures.
#
# The pruned walk, not the whole descent
#   composition/remainder_frontier.sqlc is the walk the remainder takes: it stops at the first
#   settled node on each path. composition/descent.sqlc runs on to the leaves, so an unsettled node
#   below a settled one would contribute an elimination the remainder never passed. The frontier
#   is the population algebra/settled_remainders.sqlc assigns to this relation, and it is what the
#   join reads.
#
# At the corner of its own quantity
#   `e_low` is the elimination where the quantity it was counted in is at its low, and `e_high`
#   where it is at its high. For a sum taken bound by bound those are the elimination's own low and
#   high; where that node's sum inverted and took the crossed pairing, they swap.
#   eliminations/paired.sqlc decides it, so the carried figure pairs exactly as the sum it was
#   subtracted from did.
#
# An unsized elimination is not a zero
#   An elimination filed as a typed absence has no figure, and `sum()` would skip it and report
#   the rest as the total. `unsized` says one was passed; composition/suspended_remainders.sqlc
#   suspends every remainder whose walk passes a node whose demand or nameplate sum owes nothing,
#   which covers this case and the unsearched one beside it.
#
# The emptiness is a fact about the corpus
#   So its emptiness is a fact about the corpus and not about the model. A document nesting one
#   spread conversion under another puts rows here, and a sum that omitted them would be short by
#   exactly the corrections the intermediate composer made.
-- eliminations/paired.sqlc at the nodes composition/passed_nodes.sqlc names, along a usable path.
SELECT w.root_filing AS composition, w.root_layer AS composed_layer, e.quantity,
       count(*)                                                        AS through_layers,
       sum(least(   e.at_low  * w.factor_low, e.at_low  * w.factor_high)) AS e_low,
       sum(e.mode * w.factor_mode)                                     AS e_mode,
       sum(greatest(e.at_high * w.factor_low, e.at_high * w.factor_high)) AS e_high,
       bool_or(e.absent IS NOT NULL OR e.derivation IS NOT NULL)       AS unsized
FROM      (
    :compose(composition/passed_nodes.sqlc)
) w
JOIN      (
    :compose(eliminations/paired.sqlc)
) e ON e.composition = w.filing AND e.composed_layer = w.layer
WHERE w.usable
GROUP BY w.root_filing, w.root_layer, e.quantity
